<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>The table shows the lengths, in cm (to the nearest cm), of the fish landed at a beach in Homa Bay one morning.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Length (cm)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m>–<m>{19}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20}</m>–<m>{29}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{30}</m>–<m>{39}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{40}</m>–<m>{49}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{50}</m>–<m>{59}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{60}</m>–<m>{69}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (<m>f</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{15}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{12}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{8}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>x</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>The median length is <m>{27}</m> cm. Find <m>x</m>.</p><div><m>x =</m> <fillin characters="4" name="ans1"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Work backwards through the median formula <m>\text{median} = L + \dfrac{n/2 - CF}{F} \times c</m>. The median <m>{27}</m> cm lies in the class <m>{20}</m>–<m>{29}</m>, so <m>L = {19.5}</m>, <m>CF = {15}</m>, <m>F = {12}</m> and <m>c = 10</m>. The unknown <m>x</m> comes after this class, so it changes <m>n</m> but not <m>CF</m> or <m>F</m>: <m>n = {44} + x</m>.</p><p><me>{27} = {19.5} + \frac{({44} + x)/2 - {15} }{ {12} } \times 10</me>so <m>({44} + x)/2 - {15} = ({27} - {19.5}) \times {12} \div 10 = {9}</m>, giving <m>({44} + x)/2 = {24}</m>, <m>{44} + x = {48}</m> and <m>x = {4}</m>.</p><p>Check: with <m>x = {4}</m>, <m>n = {48}</m>, and position <m>{24}</m> does lie in the class <m>{20}</m>–<m>{29}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>4</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>